=== email subject
[Action needed by 12 Oct 2026] Microsoft Windows and Microsoft Windows Server: actively exploited flaw (CVE-2026-81963)
=== email body
What's affected:
  Microsoft Windows (desktop: Windows 10, 11, and every older release still running somewhere in the building)
  Microsoft Windows Server (including the domain controller under the stairs that nobody dares to reboot)
  Patchtacio matched this by product name and has not checked whether your version is affected.

Why it matters:
  Attackers are already using this flaw: Microsoft Windows Common Log File System (CLFS) Driver Heap-Based Buffer Overflow Vulnerability (CVE-2026-81963). CISA added it to its list of exploited vulnerabilities on 28 Sep 2026.
  Fortinet FortiOS, FortiManager and FortiAnalyzer contain an authentication bypass that may allow an attacker with a FortiCloud account to log into other devices.

What to do by 12 Oct 2026:
  1. Update: check the vendor advisory for the fixed version: https://fortiguard.fortinet.com/psirt/FG-IR-26-060
  2. If you cannot update yet, follow CISA's required action: "Apply mitigations per vendor instructions, follow applicable BOD 22-01 guidance for cloud services, or discontinue use of the product if mitigations are unavailable."
  3. If neither is possible, disconnect it or restrict who can reach it until you can update.
  CISA set 12 Oct 2026 as the deadline for US government agencies. Use it as a guide to how urgent this is.

Links:
  Vendor advisory: https://fortiguard.fortinet.com/psirt/FG-IR-26-060
  CISA KEV entry: https://www.cisa.gov/known-exploited-vulnerabilities-catalog?search_api_fulltext=CVE-2026-81963
  NVD: https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-81963

--
When you have dealt with it, run: patchtacio ack CVE-2026-81963
Patchtacio then stops reminding you about it.
You get this alert because Microsoft Windows (desktop: Windows 10, 11, and every older release still running somewhere in the building) and Microsoft Windows Server (including the domain controller under the stairs that nobody dares to reboot) are on your Patchtacio product list.
